                <pb facs="1044" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg924"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660c. 11212/34</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stetson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-24">May 24, 1928</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        16.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1752</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to the Department’s telegraphic
                    Instruction No. 29 of April 17, 7 P.M.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1014-f1"/>
                    relative to American indirect shipments into Poland, I now have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a memorandum of a conversation between myself and Mr. Allen on
                    the one hand, and Mr. Kwiatkowski, Minister of Industry and Commerce, and Mr.
                    Dolezal, Vice Minister, on the other. The Department will find the memorandum in
                    question self-explanatory.</p>
                <p>I shall have the honor to keep the Department informed of the results of any
                    future conversations which I may have with Mr. Kwiatkowski on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Stetson,
                    Jr.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1014-a1.xml" xpointer="d1014-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
